# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With SQOA Solver by JIJ, you can solve large combinatorial optimization problems on IBM&reg; quantum computers. The solver is based on the Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) [\\[1\\]](#references). Unlike quantum algorithms that use a one-to-one mapping between classical decision variables and qubits, SQOA Solver can handle optimization problems with more variables than the number of qubits available on current quantum devices. Its sampling-based design also makes it less sensitive to the physical noise on current quantum hardware. Together, these features make SQOA Solver well suited to optimization problems at this stage of quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Dengan SQOA Solver dari JIJ, kamu bisa menyelesaikan masalah optimisasi kombinatorial berskala besar di komputer kuantum IBM&reg;. Solver ini berbasis Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) [\\[1\\]](#references). Berbeda dengan algoritma kuantum yang memakai pemetaan satu-ke-satu antara variabel keputusan klasik dan qubit, SQOA Solver bisa menangani masalah optimisasi dengan jumlah variabel lebih banyak daripada jumlah qubit yang tersedia di perangkat kuantum saat ini. Desainnya yang berbasis sampling juga membuatnya kurang sensitif terhadap noise fisik pada hardware kuantum saat ini. Gabungan fitur-fitur ini membuat SQOA Solver cocok untuk masalah optimisasi pada tahap komputasi kuantum sekarang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solver handles Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) problems given as a classical mathematical formulation, and it automatically maps the classical formulation into the quantum setting. You can also convert constrained problems into unconstrained ones by using the penalty method.\n"
msgstr "Solver ini menangani masalah Quadratic Unconstrained Binary Optimization (QUBO) yang diberikan sebagai formulasi matematika klasik, lalu otomatis memetakan formulasi klasik itu ke ranah kuantum. Kamu juga bisa mengubah masalah berkendala menjadi masalah tanpa kendala dengan metode penalti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following sections describe the solver's workflow, benchmark results, and end-to-end examples that model problems with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/) and, optionally, Open Mathematical prograMming eXchange (OMMX). [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) is an open data format and SDK that simplifies the exchange of optimization problems between software tools.\n"
msgstr "Bagian-bagian berikut menjelaskan alur kerja solver, hasil benchmark, dan contoh end-to-end yang memodelkan masalah dengan [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper/) dan, secara opsional, Open Mathematical prograMming eXchange (OMMX). [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/) adalah format data terbuka sekaligus SDK yang menyederhanakan pertukaran masalah optimisasi antar perangkat lunak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi {#description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver implements the Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) and surrounds it with classical preprocessing and postprocessing. This section explains the SQOA framework and how it differs from the Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA).\n"
msgstr "SQOA Solver mengimplementasikan Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) dan membungkusnya dengan preprocessing dan postprocessing klasik. Bagian ini menjelaskan kerangka SQOA dan apa bedanya dengan Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following figure shows a schematic of the SQOA Solver workflow.\n"
"![Schematic of the SQOA Solver workflow, from classical preprocessing through SQOA sampling to postprocessing and local search](/docs/images/guides/jij-sqoa-solver/sqoa-workflow.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"Gambar berikut menunjukkan skema alur kerja SQOA Solver.\n"
"![Skema alur kerja SQOA Solver, dari preprocessing klasik melalui sampling SQOA hingga postprocessing dan pencarian lokal](/docs/images/guides/jij-sqoa-solver/sqoa-workflow.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SQOA framework {#the-sqoa-framework}"
msgstr "Kerangka SQOA {#the-sqoa-framework}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA is a sampling-based framework for combinatorial optimization [\\[1\\]](#references). It combines two techniques: Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[2\\]](#references), which encodes the problem in a quantum relaxation, and sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) [\\[3\\]](#references), also known as quantum-selected configuration interaction (QSCI) [\\[4\\]](#references), which uses the quantum computer only to sample bitstrings and finds the low-energy state on a classical computer. SQOA is a framework in the sense that it fixes this combination but leaves the details to each implementation, such as how the variables are assigned to qubits and which circuits generate the samples.\n"
msgstr "SQOA adalah kerangka berbasis sampling untuk optimisasi kombinatorial [\\[1\\]](#references). Kerangka ini menggabungkan dua teknik: Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[2\\]](#references), yang menyandikan masalah dalam quantum relaxation, dan sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) [\\[3\\]](#references), yang juga dikenal sebagai quantum-selected configuration interaction (QSCI) [\\[4\\]](#references), yang memakai komputer kuantum hanya untuk mengambil sampel bitstring dan mencari keadaan berenergi rendah di komputer klasik. SQOA disebut kerangka karena menetapkan kombinasi ini tetapi menyerahkan detailnya ke tiap implementasi, seperti cara variabel ditugaskan ke qubit dan circuit mana yang menghasilkan sampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum relaxation with QRAO.** QAOA and other Ising-based approaches represent each binary variable by the $Z$ operator of its qubit. QRAO also uses the $X$ and $Y$ operators. With a (3,1) quantum random access code (QRAC), up to three binary variables share one qubit, and each variable is represented by a different Pauli operator.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum relaxation dengan QRAO.** QAOA dan pendekatan berbasis Ising lainnya merepresentasikan setiap variabel biner dengan operator $Z$ dari qubit-nya. QRAO juga memakai operator $X$ dan $Y$. Dengan (3,1) quantum random access code (QRAC), hingga tiga variabel biner berbagi satu qubit, dan setiap variabel direpresentasikan oleh operator Pauli yang berbeda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The QUBO then becomes a relaxed Hamiltonian that needs fewer qubits than the Ising Hamiltonian. Variables that interact in the QUBO must be placed on different qubits. If they shared a qubit, the product of their Pauli operators would reduce to a single operator on that qubit (for example, $XY = iZ$), and the relaxed Hamiltonian would no longer represent their interaction.\n"
msgstr "  QUBO kemudian menjadi Hamiltonian relaxed yang membutuhkan lebih sedikit qubit daripada Hamiltonian Ising. Variabel yang berinteraksi di QUBO harus ditempatkan pada qubit yang berbeda. Kalau mereka berbagi satu qubit, hasil kali operator Pauli-nya akan menyusut menjadi satu operator pada qubit itu (misalnya, $XY = iZ$), dan Hamiltonian relaxed tidak lagi merepresentasikan interaksi mereka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The assignment of variables to qubits therefore determines both the number of qubits and the quality of the relaxation, and SQOA Solver designs this assignment in its preprocessing.\n"
"- **Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD).** The quantum computer first prepares a quantum state that overlaps with low-energy states of the relaxed Hamiltonian and then samples bitstrings from it. A classical computer projects the relaxed Hamiltonian onto the subspace spanned by the sampled bitstrings and diagonalizes it to approximate the ground state.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Karena itu, penugasan variabel ke qubit menentukan jumlah qubit sekaligus kualitas relaxation, dan SQOA Solver merancang penugasan ini pada tahap preprocessing-nya.\n"
"- **Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD).** Komputer kuantum lebih dulu menyiapkan keadaan kuantum yang beririsan dengan keadaan berenergi rendah dari Hamiltonian relaxed, lalu mengambil sampel bitstring darinya. Komputer klasik memproyeksikan Hamiltonian relaxed ke subruang yang direntang oleh bitstring hasil sampling dan mendiagonalkannya untuk mengaproksimasi ground state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Because the relaxed Hamiltonian is non-diagonal, the diagonalization combines the sampled bitstrings into a superposition. With a diagonal Ising Hamiltonian, every bitstring is already an eigenstate, and the diagonalization would only select the best sample. The same approach has been applied to large-scale problems in quantum chemistry.\n"
msgstr "  Karena Hamiltonian relaxed bersifat non-diagonal, diagonalisasi menggabungkan bitstring hasil sampling menjadi superposisi. Pada Hamiltonian Ising yang diagonal, setiap bitstring sudah merupakan eigenstate, dan diagonalisasi hanya akan memilih sampel terbaik. Pendekatan yang sama sudah diterapkan pada masalah berskala besar di kimia kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The approximate ground state obtained by SQD does not directly correspond to a classical solution of the original problem, so the classical solution must be decoded from it. Because this state is computed on a classical computer, the decoding, called rounding, is classical postprocessing. SQOA Solver uses decoding techniques designed to obtain better classical solutions heuristically.\n"
msgstr "Ground state aproksimasi yang diperoleh dari SQD tidak langsung sesuai dengan solusi klasik dari masalah aslinya, jadi solusi klasik harus didekode darinya. Karena keadaan ini dihitung di komputer klasik, dekode yang disebut rounding ini merupakan postprocessing klasik. SQOA Solver memakai teknik dekode yang dirancang untuk memperoleh solusi klasik yang lebih baik secara heuristik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following table compares SQOA with QAOA, a common variational approach to the same class of problems.\n"
msgstr "Tabel berikut membandingkan SQOA dengan QAOA, pendekatan variasional umum untuk kelas masalah yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| &nbsp; | QAOA | SQOA |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Qubits for $n$ binary variables | $n$ | One qubit holds up to three of the variables. The exact number depends on the problem structure |\n"
"| Use of the QPU | Repeatedly estimates the energy of parameterized circuits inside a classical optimization loop | Only samples bitstrings. No circuit parameters are trained on the QPU |\n"
"| From samples to a solution | Selects the best measured bitstring | Diagonalizes the relaxed Hamiltonian in the sampled subspace on a classical computer and rounds the resulting state |\n"
msgstr ""
"| &nbsp; | QAOA | SQOA |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Qubit untuk $n$ variabel biner | $n$ | Satu qubit memuat hingga tiga variabel. Jumlah pastinya bergantung pada struktur masalah |\n"
"| Penggunaan QPU | Berulang kali mengestimasi energi circuit berparameter di dalam loop optimisasi klasik | Hanya mengambil sampel bitstring. Tidak ada parameter circuit yang dilatih di QPU |\n"
"| Dari sampel ke solusi | Memilih bitstring terukur terbaik | Mendiagonalkan Hamiltonian relaxed di subruang hasil sampling pada komputer klasik dan melakukan rounding pada keadaan yang dihasilkan |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Around SQOA-QR, SQOA Solver adds classical processing. Its preprocessing fixes variables whose optimal values can be determined in advance and designs the assignment of variables to qubits. Its postprocessing refines the rounded solution with a local search, which you can turn off with `postprocessing_level=0`.\n"
msgstr "Di sekeliling SQOA-QR, SQOA Solver menambahkan pemrosesan klasik. Preprocessing-nya menetapkan variabel yang nilai optimalnya bisa ditentukan sebelumnya dan merancang penugasan variabel ke qubit. Postprocessing-nya memperhalus solusi hasil rounding dengan pencarian lokal, yang bisa kamu matikan dengan `postprocessing_level=0`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"  Performance can depend on both the problem instance and subsequent processing steps. In some cases, classical samples and quantum-generated samples might achieve similar final solution quality after equivalent postprocessing. Evaluation should therefore consider the complete optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"  Performa bisa bergantung pada instans masalah dan langkah pemrosesan selanjutnya. Dalam beberapa kasus, sampel klasik dan sampel hasil kuantum mungkin mencapai kualitas solusi akhir yang mirip setelah postprocessing yang setara. Karena itu, evaluasi harus mempertimbangkan seluruh alur kerja optimisasi.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following benchmark metrics provide a general indication of solution quality, qubit compression, and execution time across selected problem sizes and structures. The table lists a selection of [Maximum Independent Set instances](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) from the Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB) and two 3-regular MaxCut instances. You can load the QOBLIB instances as `ommx.v1.Instance` objects, together with their optimal solutions, by using the [ommx-quantum-benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/) package.\n"
msgstr "Metrik benchmark berikut memberi gambaran umum tentang kualitas solusi, kompresi qubit, dan waktu eksekusi pada berbagai ukuran dan struktur masalah. Tabel ini memuat beberapa [instans Maximum Independent Set](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) dari Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB) dan dua instans MaxCut 3-regular. Kamu bisa memuat instans QOBLIB sebagai objek `ommx.v1.Instance`, beserta solusi optimalnya, dengan paket [ommx-quantum-benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each instance was run 10 times on an IBM Heron r2 processor. `Number of qubits` counts the qubits actually used on hardware after preprocessing and QRAC encoding. The compression ratio is instance-dependent. `Approximation ratio` (AR) reports the quality of the best solution found over the 10 runs:\n"
msgstr "Setiap instans dijalankan 10 kali pada prosesor IBM Heron r2. `Number of qubits` menghitung qubit yang benar-benar dipakai di hardware setelah preprocessing dan penyandian QRAC. Rasio kompresi bergantung pada instansnya. `Approximation ratio` (AR) melaporkan kualitas solusi terbaik yang ditemukan dalam 10 kali jalan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{AR} = \\frac{C_{\\textrm{best}}}{C_{\\textrm{opt}}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{AR} = \\frac{C_{\\textrm{best}}}{C_{\\textrm{opt}}},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $C_{\\textrm{best}}$ is the best objective value found and $C_{\\textrm{opt}}$ is the known optimal objective value. All instances are maximization problems with a positive optimal value, so AR is at most 100%, and 100% in the `Approximation ratio` column indicates that the solver found an optimal solution. `Total time` is the average combined QPU and CPU time per run. `QPU time` is the average IBM Quantum Compute usage per run.\n"
msgstr "dengan $C_{\\textrm{best}}$ adalah nilai objektif terbaik yang ditemukan dan $C_{\\textrm{opt}}$ adalah nilai objektif optimal yang diketahui. Semua instans adalah masalah maksimisasi dengan nilai optimal positif, jadi AR paling besar 100%, dan 100% pada kolom `Approximation ratio` menunjukkan solver menemukan solusi optimal. `Total time` adalah rata-rata gabungan waktu QPU dan CPU per jalan. `QPU time` adalah rata-rata pemakaian IBM Quantum Compute per jalan.\n"

